{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792947548,"nonce":"RzVGl68Lx21QOhyZFWnVSikOCqU=","title":"wasm builds print rustc's 'unstable feature specified for -Ctarget-feature: exception-handling' on every compile","message":".cargo/config.toml passes -Ctarget-feature=+exception-handling for wasm32-wasip1, wasm32-wasip1-threads and wasm32-wasip2. The flag is required (without it ash_std links a longjmp nothing defines and the module has no exception tag). The current nightly (1.100) classes the feature as unstable, so every compile of a workspace crate for those targets prints one warning, repeated per lib and test target. It is a rustc diagnostic, not a clippy lint; CI lint passes with it.\n\nTried: -Zllvm-target-feature=+exception-handling instead (reaches LLVM without rustc's check). It silences the warning on a one-file crate but every wasm build fails with 'mixing -Zllvm-target-feature will cause an ABI mismatch in crate X', because the flag reaches every dependency and the precompiled std does not carry it. -A for the lint name did nothing: the warning is not a lint. -Ctarget-cpu=bleeding-edge would also enable it but turns on SIMD, tail calls and more for every wasm build.\n\nRevisit when the feature is stabilised in rustc, or if rustc grows a way to allow it; until then the warning is expected.","files":null}]}